          "role": "tutor",
          "content": "`member_id` is the identifier for a member. `team_id` refers to a key in the `Teams` table, indicating which team the member belongs to. We use both because one identifies the member, while the other connects that member to a team.\n\nAri has `member_id` 1 and `team_id` 10; Bo has `member_id` 2 and also `team_id` 10. Their different member identifiers distinguish them, while the shared team_id connects both to Cedar. A foreign-key column such as team_id does not have to be unique.\n\nCheck: if a new member joins Cedar, should that person receive a new `member_id`, a new `team_id`, or both?",
