          "conversation_id": "conversation-2c29003d-871f-4200-9508-b53ccac377a9",
          "role": "tutor",
          "content": "A foreign key links a row to a key in another table, but it does not require its values to be unique. So several members can belong to the same team. The members are distinguished by their primary key, member_id.\n\nIn the example, Ari and Bo both have team_id 10, which references Cedar. That is valid because team_id identifies their shared team, while member_id 1 and 2 identify them individually.\n\nQuick check: which column identifies Ari and Bo as separate members?",
